    <statement><p>Suppose <m>\displaystyle f(x,y,z) = \frac{1}{\sqrt{x^2+y^2+z^2}}</m> 
and  <m>W</m> is the bottom half of a sphere of radius <m>4</m>.  
Enter <m>\rho</m> as <em>rho,</em> <m>\phi</m> as 
<em>phi,</em> and <m>\theta</m> as 
<em>theta.</em></p>
<p>(a) As an iterated integral,</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle 
\iiint\limits_{W} f \, dV 
=
\int_A^B \!\! \int_C^D \!\! \int_E^F</m>
<fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/>
<m>d\rho \, d\phi \, d\theta</m></p>
<p>with limits of integration</p>
<p>A = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>B = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p>C = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
<p>D = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
<p>E = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0006"/></p>
<p>F = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0007"/></p>
<p>(b) Evaluate the integral.
<fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0008"/></p>
</statement>
